    "notes": "Fourteen occupied PMTiles footprints establish the Water Training School courts, inland gallery, waterfront pavilions and the three northern ranges in the Water Village court. The native shoreline, ponds and public paths are retained. Individual room names, heights and courtyard paving are approximate. The small entry gate and fence lack a mapped footprint. The south range has a recessed timber-and-glass front, an open veranda, irregular stone infill and a narrow central step. The park festival photograph shows that facade through the separate gate. The exact gate setback remains approximate. The two rear ranges use the ridge lines visible in the aerial photograph and masonry gables observed in the 2003 Water Village field photograph. This is a reconstruction of their roof ends. Current room uses and individual facades are unverified."
  },
